  "scope": "Real full tick; native Canvas and browser DOM stubbed; frames of 1/64 s; a desk of 1440×900 (the stories at 1900×810); the worker of Wings headless thinking sixteen rehearsed frames a frame. With Facet's rules taken out and no budget, the tour and the chain through every page from every other are Cohort's, the world and every drawing command, frame by frame. With the rules alone (no budget) over the tour and the chain, every side a cell shares with the sea runs across or down the page (on Cohort they run at every angle), a frame costs less at the 90th percentile and fewer frames run over 16 ms, and fewer frames end with the auction more than 1% off a claim, in shorter runs. On the chain and the tour nothing waits, nothing fractures, from each round that moved a cell the performance is that round's rehearsal of the move to the bit, every change has one pace, every page at rest is exact and every cell drawn its own colour. With no worker the hive thinks on the page and plays what it rehearsed. A Cue story is Cohort's frame by frame; a Tell and a Tell II story run to their end and home without a fractured cell. Defects and the screen leaned on are reported against Cohort.",
